---
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<section class="section" id="guardrails">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">09 · Trust &amp; Safety</span>
      <h2>Generic safety + science-specific guardrails</h2>
      <p>
        AKD pairs generic LLM safety — content moderation and defense-in-depth
        review — with science-specific guardrails: factuality reasoning over
        claims and citations, the NASA Science Literature Risk taxonomy, and
        domain-aware compliance checks. Both layers are separate components in
        the stack, not behavior bolted onto agents. Teams compose them like any
        other dependency — declared at design time, run during build, and
        active at runtime.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="guard-grid">
      <div class="guard-shell">
        <h3 class="guard-shell-heading">What guardrails detect</h3>
        <p class="guard-shell-intro">A non-exhaustive view of the failure modes guardrails actively check for in scientific agent outputs:</p>
        <ul class="guard-list">
          <li>Hallucination</li>
          <li>Attribution gaps</li>
          <li>Unsupported claims</li>
          <li>Outdated confidence</li>
          <li>Overgeneralization</li>
          <li>Lack of grounding</li>
          <li>Multidisciplinary reasoning failures</li>
          <li>Consistency issues</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="guard-cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary guard-cta" href={`${baseUrl}guardrails/`}>
            Read more — paper references &amp; details →
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost guard-cta" href="https://github.com/NASA-IMPACT/akd/tree/main/guardrails" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" width="14" height="14"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8a8 8 0 0 0 5.47 7.59c.4.07.55-.17.55-.38v-1.33c-2.23.48-2.7-1.07-2.7-1.07-.36-.92-.89-1.17-.89-1.17-.73-.5.06-.49.06-.49.81.06 1.24.83 1.24.83.72 1.23 1.88.87 2.34.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.13 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82a7.7 7.7 0 0 1 4 0c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.11.16 1.93.08 2.13.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48v2.2c0 .21.15.46.55.38A8 8 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
            View on GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guard-cards">
        <div class="guard-group">
          <span class="guard-group-label">Generic safety</span>
          <div class="pill-card">
            <h4>Granite Guardian</h4>
            <p>Foundation-model content moderation — jailbreak, harm, bias, plus RAG groundedness, relevance, and answer-relevance checks. Off-the-shelf component.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pill-card">
            <h4>Defense-in-Depth</h4>
            <p>Layered checks across input, intermediate steps, and output — not a single gate.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guard-group guard-group--science">
          <span class="guard-group-label">Science-specific</span>
          <div class="pill-card">
            <h4>FactReasoner</h4>
            <p>Targeted factuality reasoning over claims, attribution, and supporting evidence in agent outputs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pill-card">
            <h4>Risk Agent</h4>
            <p>LLM-judge that classifies and explains risks against the IBM Risk Atlas and the NASA Science Literature Risk taxonomy.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pill-card">
            <h4>NASA Science Literature Risk Taxonomy</h4>
            <p>Domain-aware risk categories tailored to scientific contexts and agent failure modes.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .guard-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
    gap: 28px;
  }
  .guard-shell {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 32px;
    background: var(--bg-0);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }
  .guard-shell-heading { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .guard-shell-intro { margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .guard-cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 22px;
  }
  .guard-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0; margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .guard-list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .guard-list li::before {
    content: "";
    width: 6px; height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .guard-cards {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
  }
  .guard-group {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .guard-group-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }
  .guard-group--science .guard-group-label {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .guard-cards .pill-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 18px 20px;
    background: var(--bg-0);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04), 0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  }
  .guard-group--science .pill-card {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .guard-cards .pill-card h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .guard-cards .pill-card p { font-size: 13.5px; margin: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .guard-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .guard-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
